DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with all three
  of --exec-mode, --exec-logging, AND --exec-init for the vulnerable endpoint
  to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query parameter is buffered into a
  snprintf-constructed "sh -c '<cmd>'" string before being passed to system(),
  with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — three globals, utility function):
  mechanism:  Three CLI flags (--exec-mode, --exec-logging, --exec-init),
              each stored in a separate global int. A utility function
              exec_is_ready() returns non-zero only when all three are set.
  check:      `exec_is_ready() && strncmp(raw_uri, "/exec", 5) == 0`
  complexity: three flags, three globals, one gate function

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req.raw_uri (set before url_decode)
  path:       process() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts substring after "cmd=" via strncmp()
              snprintf builds: `sh -c '<cmd>' 2>/dev/null`
              system() executes the constructed string
  transforms: one snprintf indirection; shell wrapping adds sh -c layer

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (tiny.c, injected before process())

CHANGED FILES:
  tiny.c — 6 hunks:
    1. http_request struct:  added raw_uri[512] field
    2. globals:              added exec_mode, exec_logging, exec_initialized,
                             exec_is_ready() utility function
    3. parse_request():      added strncpy of uri into req->raw_uri before processing
    4. send_exec_reply():    new helper function using write()
    5. handle_exec():        new function with snprintf shell wrap, then system()
    6. process():            added C3 exec route before normal file serving
    7. main():               replaced positional-only arg parsing with flag+positional parser

EXPLOIT:
  build:   gcc -o tiny tiny.c
  start:   ./tiny --exec-mode --exec-logging --exec-init /tmp/www 18022
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18022/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting any one of the three flags causes /exec to return 404.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    Use a write-to-file payload (no single quotes in the payload, as snprintf
    wraps in sh -c '...' — use > redirection directly, e.g. id>/tmp/pwned).
  - The server forks 10 worker children; the exec route runs in a child process.
  - raw_uri is captured before url_decode, so percent-encoded payloads are
    not automatically decoded (use literal characters in the payload).
